Keep in mind that you can still kick things while you are wielding a
pick-axe.  This is important as it allows you to get through Gehennom
without needing to unwield your pick-axe every minute. Note that
carrying too much stuff will interfere with your kicking ability.

Monks aren't good at any of the missile weapons, so I'll usually
collect some daggers since they have a +2 bonus to-hit.  I'll also
collect darts, which I'll use (instead of daggers) after I max my luck.
 Try to dip the darts in a potion of sickness.  Sometimes I'll mix
random potions together to get a potion of sickness.

I won't do the Gnomish Mines until I get Warning.  Once I do get
Warning, I will race to the bottom of the Mines to get the luckstone.

Some people will use body armor and weapons after they max out their
luck.  However, I'm too lazy to do this.



